<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>An Offline Inverse Reinforcement Learning Approach for Token-level MDPs</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here we provide a complete derivation on the offline IRL approach presented in <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Reward Learning from Inverse Reinforcement Learning ‣ 3 Finding the Endogenous Reward Within the Language Model ‣ Generalist Reward Models: Found Inside Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We start from the minimax formulation of maximum entropy IRL shown in Eq.(<a href="#S2.E5" title="Equation 5 ‣ 2.4 Inverse Reinforcement Learning ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Generalist Reward Models: Found Inside Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>). As discussed in <a href="#S2.SS4" title="2.4 Inverse Reinforcement Learning ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Generalist Reward Models: Found Inside Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.4</span></a>, the inner optimization is the problem of maximum entropy reinforcement learning with reward <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Haarnoja et al., 2017</a>, <a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Geist et al., 2019</a>]</cite>, admitting the following solution:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi^{\star}_{r}(a_{h}|s_{h})=\frac{\exp\left(Q^{\star}_{r}(s_{h},a_{h})/\alpha\right)}{\sum_{a^{\prime}_{h}\in{\mathcal{V}}}\exp\left(Q^{\star}_{r}(s_{h},a^{\prime}_{h})/\alpha\right)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi^{\star}_{r}(a_{h}|s_{h})=\frac{\exp\left(Q^{\star}_{r}(s_{h},a_{h})/\alpha\right)}{\sum_{a^{\prime}_{h}\in{\mathcal{V}}}\exp\left(Q^{\star}_{r}(s_{h},a^{\prime}_{h})/\alpha\right)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\star}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\star}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> is the entropy-regularized optimal Q-value function with reward <math id="A1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, which is defined as <math id="A1.p2.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Q^{\star}_{r}(s_{h},a_{h}):=r_{h}(s_{h},a_{h})+\max_{\pi}\mathbb{E}[\sum_{h^{\prime}=h+1}^{H}r_{h^{\prime}}(s_{h^{\prime}},a_{h^{\prime}})+\alpha H(\pi(\cdot|s_{h^{\prime}}))|s_{h},a_{h}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>H</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>r</mi><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\star}_{r}(s_{h},a_{h}):=r_{h}(s_{h},a_{h})+\max_{\pi}\mathbb{E}[\sum_{h^{\prime}=h+1}^{H}r_{h^{\prime}}(s_{h^{\prime}},a_{h^{\prime}})+\alpha H(\pi(\cdot|s_{h^{\prime}}))|s_{h},a_{h}]</annotation></semantics></math> for an arbitrary <math id="A1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s_{h},a_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s_{h},a_{h})</annotation></semantics></math> in step <math id="A1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>. In addition, if we define the entropy-regularized Bellman operator as</p>
<table id="A1.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle[{\mathcal{T}}Q](s_{h},a_{h}):=r(s_{h},a_{h})+\alpha\log\left(\sum_{a_{h+1}\in{\mathcal{V}}}\exp\left(Q(s_{h+1},a_{h+1})\right)/\alpha\right)\;\text{with}\;s_{h+1}=P(s_{h},a_{h})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>with</mtext><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle[{\mathcal{T}}Q](s_{h},a_{h}):=r(s_{h},a_{h})+\alpha\log\left(\sum_{a_{h+1}\in{\mathcal{V}}}\exp\left(Q(s_{h+1},a_{h+1})\right)/\alpha\right)\;\text{with}\;s_{h+1}=P(s_{h},a_{h}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">we have that <math id="A1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\star}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\star}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> is the fixed point of <math id="A1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{T}}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="A1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\star}_{r}(s_{h},a_{h})=[{\mathcal{T}}Q^{\star}_{r}](s_{h},a_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\star}_{r}(s_{h},a_{h})=[{\mathcal{T}}Q^{\star}_{r}](s_{h},a_{h})</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Geist et al., 2019</a>]</cite>. Substituting the inner problem solution of Eq.(<a href="#A1.E14" title="Equation 14 ‣ Appendix A An Offline Inverse Reinforcement Learning Approach for Token-level MDPs ‣ Generalist Reward Models: Found Inside Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>) into Eq.(<a href="#S2.E5" title="Equation 5 ‣ 2.4 Inverse Reinforcement Learning ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Generalist Reward Models: Found Inside Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) yields a single maximization problem.</p>
<table id="A1.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{r}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{h=1}^{H}r(s^{i}_{h},a^{i}_{h})-\alpha\mathbb{E}_{s_{1}\sim\rho}\left[\log\left(\sum_{a_{1}\in{\mathcal{V}}}\exp\left(Q^{\star}_{r}(s_{1},a_{1})/\alpha\right)\right)\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>r</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{r}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{h=1}^{H}r(s^{i}_{h},a^{i}_{h})-\alpha\mathbb{E}_{s_{1}\sim\rho}\left[\log\left(\sum_{a_{1}\in{\mathcal{V}}}\exp\left(Q^{\star}_{r}(s_{1},a_{1})/\alpha\right)\right)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">Furthermore, following the IRL approach inverse soft Q-learning <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Garg et al., 2021</a>]</cite>, we take the change-of-variable, replacing the reward function with the Q-value function based on the so-called inverse Bellman operator.</p>
<table id="A1.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r(s_{h},a_{h})=[{\mathcal{T}}^{-1}Q](s_{h},a_{h}):=Q(s_{h},a_{h})-\alpha\log\left(\sum_{a_{h+1}\in{\mathcal{V}}}\exp\left(Q(s_{h+1},a_{h+1})\right)/\alpha\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r(s_{h},a_{h})=[{\mathcal{T}}^{-1}Q](s_{h},a_{h}):=Q(s_{h},a_{h})-\alpha\log\left(\sum_{a_{h+1}\in{\mathcal{V}}}\exp\left(Q(s_{h+1},a_{h+1})\right)/\alpha\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.5" class="ltx_p">Then we obtain the final objective regarding the Q-value function based on dataset <math id="A1.p2.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{D}=\{(x^{i},a^{i}_{1:H})\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}=\{(x^{i},a^{i}_{1:H})\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="A1.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>Q</mi></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{h=1}^{H}\left(Q(s^{i}_{h},a^{i}_{h})-\alpha\log\bigg(\sum_{a_{h+1}\in{\mathcal{V}}}\exp\left(Q(s^{i}_{h+1},a_{h+1})\right)/\alpha\bigg)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{h=1}^{H}\left(Q(s^{i}_{h},a^{i}_{h})-\alpha\log\bigg(\sum_{a_{h+1}\in{\mathcal{V}}}\exp\left(Q(s^{i}_{h+1},a_{h+1})\right)/\alpha\bigg)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\alpha\mathbb{E}_{s_{1}\sim\rho}\left[\log\left(\sum_{a_{1}\in{\mathcal{V}}}\exp\left(Q(s_{1},a_{1})/\alpha\right)\right)\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\alpha\mathbb{E}_{s_{1}\sim\rho}\left[\log\left(\sum_{a_{1}\in{\mathcal{V}}}\exp\left(Q(s_{1},a_{1})/\alpha\right)\right)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.6" class="ltx_p">For the second term in the above objective, we leverage the telescoping argument and obtain that</p>
<table id="A1.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\alpha\mathbb{E}_{s_{1}\sim\rho}\left[\log\left(\sum_{a_{1}\in{\mathcal{V}}}\exp\left(Q(s_{1},a_{1})/\alpha\right)\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\alpha\mathbb{E}_{s_{1}\sim\rho}\left[\log\left(\sum_{a_{1}\in{\mathcal{V}}}\exp\left(Q(s_{1},a_{1})/\alpha\right)\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\alpha\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim\pi^{\operatorname{E}}}\left[\sum_{h=1}^{H}\log\left(\sum_{a_{h}\in{\mathcal{V}}}\exp\left(Q(s_{h},a_{h})/\alpha\right)\right)-\log\left(\sum_{a_{h+1}\in{\mathcal{V}}}\exp\left(Q(s_{h+1},a_{h+1})/\alpha\right)\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\alpha\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim\pi^{\operatorname{E}}}\left[\sum_{h=1}^{H}\log\left(\sum_{a_{h}\in{\mathcal{V}}}\exp\left(Q(s_{h},a_{h})/\alpha\right)\right)-\log\left(\sum_{a_{h+1}\in{\mathcal{V}}}\exp\left(Q(s_{h+1},a_{h+1})/\alpha\right)\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.7" class="ltx_p">Plugging the above equation into the objective function yields that</p>
<table id="A1.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>Q</mi></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{h=1}^{H}\left(Q(s^{i}_{h},a^{i}_{h})-\alpha\log\bigg(\sum_{a_{h+1}\in{\mathcal{V}}}\exp\left(Q(s^{i}_{h+1},a_{h+1})\right)/\alpha\bigg)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{h=1}^{H}\left(Q(s^{i}_{h},a^{i}_{h})-\alpha\log\bigg(\sum_{a_{h+1}\in{\mathcal{V}}}\exp\left(Q(s^{i}_{h+1},a_{h+1})\right)/\alpha\bigg)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\alpha\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim\pi^{\operatorname{E}}}\left[\sum_{h=1}^{H}\log\left(\sum_{a_{h}\in{\mathcal{V}}}\exp\left(Q(s_{h},a_{h})/\alpha\right)\right)-\log\left(\sum_{a_{h+1}\in{\mathcal{V}}}\exp\left(Q(s_{h+1},a_{h+1})/\alpha\right)\right)\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\alpha\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim\pi^{\operatorname{E}}}\left[\sum_{h=1}^{H}\log\left(\sum_{a_{h}\in{\mathcal{V}}}\exp\left(Q(s_{h},a_{h})/\alpha\right)\right)-\log\left(\sum_{a_{h+1}\in{\mathcal{V}}}\exp\left(Q(s_{h+1},a_{h+1})/\alpha\right)\right)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.8" class="ltx_p">We can leverage demonstrations <math id="A1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{D}}</annotation></semantics></math> to unbiasedly estimate the expectation term, yielding the final objective.</p>
<table id="A1.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{Q}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{h=1}^{H}\left[Q(s^{i}_{h},a^{i}_{h})-\alpha\log\bigg(\sum_{a_{h}\in{\mathcal{V}}}\exp\left(Q(s^{i}_{h},a_{h})\right)/\alpha\bigg)\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>Q</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{Q}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{h=1}^{H}\left[Q(s^{i}_{h},a^{i}_{h})-\alpha\log\bigg(\sum_{a_{h}\in{\mathcal{V}}}\exp\left(Q(s^{i}_{h},a_{h})\right)/\alpha\bigg)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Ommited Proofs</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmprop1" title="Proposition 1. ‣ 3.2 Next-Token Prediction Recovers the IRL Solution ‣ 3 Finding the Endogenous Reward Within the Language Model ‣ Generalist Reward Models: Found Inside Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof is mainly based on the definition. Since <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{\pi}(\cdot|s_{h})=\mathrm{softmax}(\widehat{f}(s_{h},\cdot);\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>softmax</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>;</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}(\cdot|s_{h})=\mathrm{softmax}(\widehat{f}(s_{h},\cdot);\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math> is the optimal solution to next-token prediction in Eq.(<a href="#S2.E1" title="Equation 1 ‣ 2.2 Next-token Prediction for Training LLMs ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Generalist Reward Models: Found Inside Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{\pi}\in\mathop{\rm argmax}_{\pi}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{h=1}^{H}\log\left(\pi\left(a^{i}_{t}|x^{i},a^{i}_{1:h-1}\right)\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.1389em">∈</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">argmax</mo><mi>π</mi></munder><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{\pi}\in\mathop{\rm argmax}_{\pi}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{h=1}^{H}\log\left(\pi\left(a^{i}_{t}|x^{i},a^{i}_{1:h-1}\right)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">This immediately implies that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{f}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\in\mathop{\rm argmax}_{f}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{h=1}^{H}\log\left(\frac{\exp(f(s^{i}_{h},a^{i}_{h})/\alpha)}{\sum_{a^{\prime}_{h}\in{\mathcal{V}}}\exp(f(s^{i}_{h},a^{\prime}_{h})/\alpha)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">∈</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">argmax</mo><mi>f</mi></munder><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\in\mathop{\rm argmax}_{f}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{h=1}^{H}\log\left(\frac{\exp(f(s^{i}_{h},a^{i}_{h})/\alpha)}{\sum_{a^{\prime}_{h}\in{\mathcal{V}}}\exp(f(s^{i}_{h},a^{\prime}_{h})/\alpha)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathop{\rm argmax}_{f}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{h=1}^{H}\left[f(s^{i}_{h},a^{i}_{h})-\alpha\log\bigg(\sum_{a_{h}\in{\mathcal{V}}}\exp\left(f(s^{i}_{h},a_{h})\right)/\alpha\bigg)\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">argmax</mo><mi>f</mi></munder><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathop{\rm argmax}_{f}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{h=1}^{H}\left[f(s^{i}_{h},a^{i}_{h})-\alpha\log\bigg(\sum_{a_{h}\in{\mathcal{V}}}\exp\left(f(s^{i}_{h},a_{h})\right)/\alpha\bigg)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">By comparing Eq.(<a href="#A2.E16" title="Equation 16 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix B Ommited Proofs ‣ Generalist Reward Models: Found Inside Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>) and Eq.(<a href="#S3.E6" title="Equation 6 ‣ 3.1 Reward Learning from Inverse Reinforcement Learning ‣ 3 Finding the Endogenous Reward Within the Language Model ‣ Generalist Reward Models: Found Inside Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>), we can conclude that <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{f}</annotation></semantics></math> is the optimal solution to the offline IRL objective of Eq.(<a href="#S3.E6" title="Equation 6 ‣ 3.1 Reward Learning from Inverse Reinforcement Learning ‣ 3 Finding the Endogenous Reward Within the Language Model ‣ Generalist Reward Models: Found Inside Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmthm1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 4.1 Error Analysis of the Endogenous Reward. ‣ 4 Theoretical Justifications for the Endogenous Reward ‣ Generalist Reward Models: Found Inside Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Based on the property of the TV distance on Bernoulli distribution, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad D_{\mathrm{TV}}\left({\mathbb{P}}_{r^{\star}}(\cdot|\tau,\tau^{\prime}),{\mathbb{P}}_{\widehat{r}}(\cdot|\tau,\tau^{\prime})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>TV</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad D_{\mathrm{TV}}\left({\mathbb{P}}_{r^{\star}}(\cdot|\tau,\tau^{\prime}),{\mathbb{P}}_{\widehat{r}}(\cdot|\tau,\tau^{\prime})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\left(\left|{\mathbb{P}}_{r^{\star}}(\tau\succ\tau^{\prime}|\tau,\tau^{\prime})-{\mathbb{P}}_{\widehat{r}}(\tau\succ\tau^{\prime}|\tau,\tau^{\prime})\right|+\left|{\mathbb{P}}_{r^{\star}}(\tau\prec\tau^{\prime}|\tau,\tau^{\prime})-{\mathbb{P}}_{\widehat{r}}(\tau\prec\tau^{\prime}|\tau,\tau^{\prime})\right|\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>≻</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>≻</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>≺</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>≺</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\left(\left|{\mathbb{P}}_{r^{\star}}(\tau\succ\tau^{\prime}|\tau,\tau^{\prime})-{\mathbb{P}}_{\widehat{r}}(\tau\succ\tau^{\prime}|\tau,\tau^{\prime})\right|+\left|{\mathbb{P}}_{r^{\star}}(\tau\prec\tau^{\prime}|\tau,\tau^{\prime})-{\mathbb{P}}_{\widehat{r}}(\tau\prec\tau^{\prime}|\tau,\tau^{\prime})\right|\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left|{\mathbb{P}}_{r^{\star}}(\tau\succ\tau^{\prime}|\tau,\tau^{\prime})-{\mathbb{P}}_{\widehat{r}}(\tau\succ\tau^{\prime}|\tau,\tau^{\prime})\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>≻</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>≻</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left|{\mathbb{P}}_{r^{\star}}(\tau\succ\tau^{\prime}|\tau,\tau^{\prime})-{\mathbb{P}}_{\widehat{r}}(\tau\succ\tau^{\prime}|\tau,\tau^{\prime})\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left|\sigma(r^{\star}(\tau)-r^{\star}(\tau^{\prime}))-\sigma(\widehat{r}(\tau)-\widehat{r}(\tau^{\prime}))\right|." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left|\sigma(r^{\star}(\tau)-r^{\star}(\tau^{\prime}))-\sigma(\widehat{r}(\tau)-\widehat{r}(\tau^{\prime}))\right|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">For the sigmoid function, we have that <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{\prime}(x)=\sigma(x)(1-\sigma(x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{\prime}(x)=\sigma(x)(1-\sigma(x))</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(x)\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(x)\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, it is direct to have that <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\sigma^{\prime}(x)|\leq 1/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\sigma^{\prime}(x)|\leq 1/4</annotation></semantics></math>, implying that <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/4</annotation></semantics></math>-lipschitz function. Then we have that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\mathrm{TV}}\left({\mathbb{P}}_{r^{\star}}(\cdot|\tau,\tau^{\prime}),{\mathbb{P}}_{\widehat{r}}(\cdot|\tau,\tau^{\prime})\right)\leq\frac{1}{4}\left|r^{\star}(\tau)-r^{\star}(\tau^{\prime})-(\widehat{r}(\tau)-\widehat{r}(\tau^{\prime}))\right|." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>TV</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\mathrm{TV}}\left({\mathbb{P}}_{r^{\star}}(\cdot|\tau,\tau^{\prime}),{\mathbb{P}}_{\widehat{r}}(\cdot|\tau,\tau^{\prime})\right)\leq\frac{1}{4}\left|r^{\star}(\tau)-r^{\star}(\tau^{\prime})-(\widehat{r}(\tau)-\widehat{r}(\tau^{\prime}))\right|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">According to Eq.(<a href="#S3.E12" title="Equation 12 ‣ Outcome Reward. ‣ 3.3 The Endogenous Reward ‣ 3 Finding the Endogenous Reward Within the Language Model ‣ Generalist Reward Models: Found Inside Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>), we have that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r^{\star}(\tau)-r^{\star}(\tau^{\prime})=\alpha\left(\log\pi^{\operatorname{E}}(\tau|s_{1})-\log\pi^{\operatorname{E}}(\tau^{\prime}|s_{1})\right),\;\widehat{r}(\tau)-\widehat{r}(\tau^{\prime})=\alpha\left(\log\widehat{\pi}(\tau|s_{1})-\log\widehat{\pi}(\tau^{\prime}|s_{1})\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r^{\star}(\tau)-r^{\star}(\tau^{\prime})=\alpha\left(\log\pi^{\operatorname{E}}(\tau|s_{1})-\log\pi^{\operatorname{E}}(\tau^{\prime}|s_{1})\right),\;\widehat{r}(\tau)-\widehat{r}(\tau^{\prime})=\alpha\left(\log\widehat{\pi}(\tau|s_{1})-\log\widehat{\pi}(\tau^{\prime}|s_{1})\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">where the V-function in <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> can be canceled. Then we can obtain that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad D_{\mathrm{TV}}\left({\mathbb{P}}_{r^{\star}}(\cdot|\tau,\tau^{\prime}),{\mathbb{P}}_{\widehat{r}}(\cdot|\tau,\tau^{\prime})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>TV</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad D_{\mathrm{TV}}\left({\mathbb{P}}_{r^{\star}}(\cdot|\tau,\tau^{\prime}),{\mathbb{P}}_{\widehat{r}}(\cdot|\tau,\tau^{\prime})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{4}\left|r^{\star}(\tau)-r^{\star}(\tau^{\prime})-(\widehat{r}(\tau)-\widehat{r}(\tau^{\prime}))\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{4}\left|r^{\star}(\tau)-r^{\star}(\tau^{\prime})-(\widehat{r}(\tau)-\widehat{r}(\tau^{\prime}))\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{\alpha}{4}\left(\left|\log(\pi^{\operatorname{E}}(\tau|s_{1}))-\log(\widehat{\pi}(\tau|s_{1}))\right|+\left|\log(\pi^{\operatorname{E}}(\tau^{\prime}|s_{1}))-\log(\widehat{\pi}(\tau^{\prime}|s_{1}))\right|\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{\alpha}{4}\left(\left|\log(\pi^{\operatorname{E}}(\tau|s_{1}))-\log(\widehat{\pi}(\tau|s_{1}))\right|+\left|\log(\pi^{\operatorname{E}}(\tau^{\prime}|s_{1}))-\log(\widehat{\pi}(\tau^{\prime}|s_{1}))\right|\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{\alpha}{4}\left(\left|\log(\pi^{\operatorname{E}}(\tau|s_{1}))-\log(\widehat{\pi}(\tau|s_{1}))\right|+\left|\log(\pi^{\operatorname{E}}(\tau^{\prime}|s_{1}))-\log(\widehat{\pi}(\tau^{\prime}|s_{1}))\right|\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{\alpha}{4}\left(\left|\log(\pi^{\operatorname{E}}(\tau|s_{1}))-\log(\widehat{\pi}(\tau|s_{1}))\right|+\left|\log(\pi^{\operatorname{E}}(\tau^{\prime}|s_{1}))-\log(\widehat{\pi}(\tau^{\prime}|s_{1}))\right|\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{\alpha H}{2}\varepsilon_{\pi}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>π</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{\alpha H}{2}\varepsilon_{\pi}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">We complete the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmthm2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ 4.2 Error Analysis of the LLM Finetuned by the Endogenous Reward ‣ 4 Theoretical Justifications for the Endogenous Reward ‣ Generalist Reward Models: Found Inside Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">The first sub-optimality bound is exactly the error bound of behavioral cloning, variants of which have been established in the literature of imitation learning theory <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xu et al., 2020</a>, <a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rajaraman et al., 2020</a>]</cite>. First, we leverage the dual representation of policy value, i.e., <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\pi}=\sum_{h=1}^{H}\sum_{(s,a)}d^{\pi}_{h}(s,a)r_{h}(s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\pi}=\sum_{h=1}^{H}\sum_{(s,a)}d^{\pi}_{h}(s,a)r_{h}(s,a)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\pi}_{h}(s,a)={\mathbb{P}}^{\pi}(s_{h}=s,a_{h}=a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\pi}_{h}(s,a)={\mathbb{P}}^{\pi}(s_{h}=s,a_{h}=a)</annotation></semantics></math> is the probability of visiting <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s,a)</annotation></semantics></math> in step <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>. Under the assumption <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\star}_{h}(s,a)\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\star}_{h}(s,a)\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V^{\pi^{\operatorname{E}}}_{r^{\star}}-V^{\widehat{\pi}}_{r^{\star}}\leq\sum_{h=1}^{H}\left\|d^{\pi^{\operatorname{E}}}_{h}(s,a)-d^{\pi}_{h}(s,a)\right\|_{1}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V^{\pi^{\operatorname{E}}}_{r^{\star}}-V^{\widehat{\pi}}_{r^{\star}}\leq\sum_{h=1}^{H}\left\|d^{\pi^{\operatorname{E}}}_{h}(s,a)-d^{\pi}_{h}(s,a)\right\|_{1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">We leverage Lemma 4 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xu et al., 2022</a>]</cite> and obtain that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V^{\pi^{\operatorname{E}}}_{r^{\star}}-V^{\widehat{\pi}}_{r^{\star}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V^{\pi^{\operatorname{E}}}_{r^{\star}}-V^{\widehat{\pi}}_{r^{\star}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{h=1}^{H}\left\|d^{\pi^{\operatorname{E}}}_{h}(s,a)-d^{\widehat{\pi}}_{h}(s,a)\right\|_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{h=1}^{H}\left\|d^{\pi^{\operatorname{E}}}_{h}(s,a)-d^{\widehat{\pi}}_{h}(s,a)\right\|_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{h=1}^{H}\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim\pi^{\operatorname{E}}}\left[\sum_{\ell=1}^{h}\left\|\pi^{\operatorname{E}}(\cdot|s_{h})-\widehat{\pi}(\cdot|s_{h})\right\|_{1}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>h</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{h=1}^{H}\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim\pi^{\operatorname{E}}}\left[\sum_{\ell=1}^{h}\left\|\pi^{\operatorname{E}}(\cdot|s_{h})-\widehat{\pi}(\cdot|s_{h})\right\|_{1}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(a)}{\leq}\sqrt{2}\sum_{h=1}^{H}\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim\pi^{\operatorname{E}}}\left[\sum_{\ell=1}^{h}D_{\mathrm{KL}}\left(\pi^{\operatorname{E}}(\cdot|s_{h}),\widehat{\pi}(\cdot|s_{h})\right)\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">a</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>h</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(a)}{\leq}\sqrt{2}\sum_{h=1}^{H}\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim\pi^{\operatorname{E}}}\left[\sum_{\ell=1}^{h}D_{\mathrm{KL}}\left(\pi^{\operatorname{E}}(\cdot|s_{h}),\widehat{\pi}(\cdot|s_{h})\right)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">We can analyze the KL-divergence term via</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\mathrm{KL}}\left(\pi^{\operatorname{E}}(\cdot|s_{h}),\widehat{\pi}(\cdot|s_{h})\right)=\sum_{a_{h}\in{\mathcal{V}}}\pi^{\operatorname{E}}(a_{h}|s_{h})\left(\log(\pi^{\operatorname{E}}(a_{h}|s_{h}))-\log(\widehat{\pi}(a_{h}|s_{h}))\right)\leq\varepsilon_{\pi}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\mathrm{KL}}\left(\pi^{\operatorname{E}}(\cdot|s_{h}),\widehat{\pi}(\cdot|s_{h})\right)=\sum_{a_{h}\in{\mathcal{V}}}\pi^{\operatorname{E}}(a_{h}|s_{h})\left(\log(\pi^{\operatorname{E}}(a_{h}|s_{h}))-\log(\widehat{\pi}(a_{h}|s_{h}))\right)\leq\varepsilon_{\pi}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">Then we have that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V^{\pi^{\operatorname{E}}}_{r^{\star}}-V^{\widehat{\pi}}_{r^{\star}}\leq\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}H(H+1)\varepsilon_{\pi}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>π</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V^{\pi^{\operatorname{E}}}_{r^{\star}}-V^{\widehat{\pi}}_{r^{\star}}\leq\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}H(H+1)\varepsilon_{\pi},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">which proves the first sub-optimality bound.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We proceed to prove the second sub-optimality bound. Recall the formulation of the endogenous reward in the reward-shaping view.</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{r}(s_{h},a_{h})=\alpha\log\left(\widehat{\pi}(a_{h}|s_{h})\right)+V_{\widehat{Q}}(s_{h})-V_{\widehat{Q}}(s_{h+1})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{r}(s_{h},a_{h})=\alpha\log\left(\widehat{\pi}(a_{h}|s_{h})\right)+V_{\widehat{Q}}(s_{h})-V_{\widehat{Q}}(s_{h+1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">We define another reward <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{r}</annotation></semantics></math> as</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bar{r}(s_{h},a_{h}):=\alpha\log\left(\widehat{\pi}(a_{h}|s_{h})\right)+V_{Q^{\star}_{r^{\star}}}(s_{h})-V_{Q^{\star}_{r^{\star}}}(s_{h+1})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bar{r}(s_{h},a_{h}):=\alpha\log\left(\widehat{\pi}(a_{h}|s_{h})\right)+V_{Q^{\star}_{r^{\star}}}(s_{h})-V_{Q^{\star}_{r^{\star}}}(s_{h+1}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\star}_{r^{\star}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\star}_{r^{\star}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the entropy-regularized optimal Q-function with the true reward <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>. We can get that <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{r}</annotation></semantics></math> is a shaping reward of <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{r}</annotation></semantics></math> with a different potential function <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{Q^{\star}_{r^{\star}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{Q^{\star}_{r^{\star}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">With the intermediate reward <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, we decompose the sub-optimality into three parts.</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V^{\pi^{\operatorname{E}}}_{r^{\star}}-V^{\pi^{\operatorname{RL}}}_{r^{\star}}\leq V^{\pi^{\operatorname{E}}}_{r^{\star}}-V^{\pi^{\operatorname{E}}}_{\bar{r}}+V^{\pi^{\operatorname{E}}}_{\bar{r}}-V^{\pi^{\operatorname{RL}}}_{\bar{r}}+V^{\pi^{\operatorname{RL}}}_{\bar{r}}-V^{\pi^{\operatorname{RL}}}_{r^{\star}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>RL</mi></msup></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>RL</mi></msup></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>RL</mi></msup></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>RL</mi></msup></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V^{\pi^{\operatorname{E}}}_{r^{\star}}-V^{\pi^{\operatorname{RL}}}_{r^{\star}}\leq V^{\pi^{\operatorname{E}}}_{r^{\star}}-V^{\pi^{\operatorname{E}}}_{\bar{r}}+V^{\pi^{\operatorname{E}}}_{\bar{r}}-V^{\pi^{\operatorname{RL}}}_{\bar{r}}+V^{\pi^{\operatorname{RL}}}_{\bar{r}}-V^{\pi^{\operatorname{RL}}}_{r^{\star}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\operatorname{RL}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>RL</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\operatorname{RL}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the optimal policy regarding <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{r}</annotation></semantics></math>. Based on the theory on reward shaping <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ng et al., 1999</a>]</cite>, <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\operatorname{RL}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>RL</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\operatorname{RL}}</annotation></semantics></math> is also the optimal policy regarding <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, indicating that <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\pi^{\operatorname{E}}}_{\bar{r}}-V^{\pi^{\operatorname{RL}}}_{\bar{r}}\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>RL</mi></msup></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\pi^{\operatorname{E}}}_{\bar{r}}-V^{\pi^{\operatorname{RL}}}_{\bar{r}}\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we obtain that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V^{\pi^{\operatorname{E}}}_{r^{\star}}-V^{\pi^{\operatorname{RL}}}_{r^{\star}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>RL</mi></msup></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V^{\pi^{\operatorname{E}}}_{r^{\star}}-V^{\pi^{\operatorname{RL}}}_{r^{\star}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex34.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq V^{\pi^{\operatorname{E}}}_{r^{\star}}-V^{\pi^{\operatorname{E}}}_{\bar{r}}+V^{\pi^{\operatorname{RL}}}_{\bar{r}}-V^{\pi^{\operatorname{RL}}}_{r^{\star}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>RL</mi></msup></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>RL</mi></msup></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq V^{\pi^{\operatorname{E}}}_{r^{\star}}-V^{\pi^{\operatorname{E}}}_{\bar{r}}+V^{\pi^{\operatorname{RL}}}_{\bar{r}}-V^{\pi^{\operatorname{RL}}}_{r^{\star}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim\pi^{\operatorname{E}}}\left[r^{\star}(\tau)-\macc@depth\char 1\relax\macc@set@skewchar\macc@nested@a 111{r}(\tau)\right]+\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim\pi^{\operatorname{RL}}}\left[r^{\star}(\tau)-\macc@depth\char 1\relax\macc@set@skewchar\macc@nested@a 111{r}(\tau)\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mtext class="undefined">\macc@depth</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\macc@set@skewchar</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\macc@nested@a</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>111</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>RL</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mtext class="undefined">\macc@depth</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\macc@set@skewchar</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\macc@nested@a</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>111</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim\pi^{\operatorname{E}}}\left[r^{\star}(\tau)-\macc@depth\char 1\relax\macc@set@skewchar\macc@nested@a 111{r}(\tau)\right]+\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim\pi^{\operatorname{RL}}}\left[r^{\star}(\tau)-\macc@depth\char 1\relax\macc@set@skewchar\macc@nested@a 111{r}(\tau)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Based on Eq.(<a href="#S3.E12" title="Equation 12 ‣ Outcome Reward. ‣ 3.3 The Endogenous Reward ‣ 3 Finding the Endogenous Reward Within the Language Model ‣ Generalist Reward Models: Found Inside Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>), we have that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r^{\star}(\tau)-\macc@depth\char 1\relax\macc@set@skewchar\macc@nested@a 111{r}(\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mtext class="undefined">\macc@depth</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\macc@set@skewchar</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\macc@nested@a</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>111</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r^{\star}(\tau)-\macc@depth\char 1\relax\macc@set@skewchar\macc@nested@a 111{r}(\tau)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex36.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\alpha\log(\pi^{\operatorname{E}}(\tau|s_{1}))+V_{Q^{\star}_{r^{\star}}}(s_{1})-\alpha\log(\widehat{\pi}(\tau|s_{1}))-V_{Q^{\star}_{r^{\star}}}(s_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\alpha\log(\pi^{\operatorname{E}}(\tau|s_{1}))+V_{Q^{\star}_{r^{\star}}}(s_{1})-\alpha\log(\widehat{\pi}(\tau|s_{1}))-V_{Q^{\star}_{r^{\star}}}(s_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\alpha\sum_{h=1}^{H}\log(\pi^{\operatorname{E}}(a_{h}|s_{h}))-\log(\widehat{\pi}(a_{h}|s_{h}))." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\alpha\sum_{h=1}^{H}\log(\pi^{\operatorname{E}}(a_{h}|s_{h}))-\log(\widehat{\pi}(a_{h}|s_{h})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">Then we can derive that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad V^{\pi^{\operatorname{E}}}_{r^{\star}}-V^{\pi^{\operatorname{RL}}}_{r^{\star}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>RL</mi></msup></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad V^{\pi^{\operatorname{E}}}_{r^{\star}}-V^{\pi^{\operatorname{RL}}}_{r^{\star}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim\pi^{\operatorname{E}}}\left[r^{\star}(\tau)-\macc@depth\char 1\relax\macc@set@skewchar\macc@nested@a 111{r}(\tau)\right]+\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim\pi^{\operatorname{RL}}}\left[r^{\star}(\tau)-\macc@depth\char 1\relax\macc@set@skewchar\macc@nested@a 111{r}(\tau)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mtext class="undefined">\macc@depth</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\macc@set@skewchar</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\macc@nested@a</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>111</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>RL</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mtext class="undefined">\macc@depth</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\macc@set@skewchar</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\macc@nested@a</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>111</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim\pi^{\operatorname{E}}}\left[r^{\star}(\tau)-\macc@depth\char 1\relax\macc@set@skewchar\macc@nested@a 111{r}(\tau)\right]+\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim\pi^{\operatorname{RL}}}\left[r^{\star}(\tau)-\macc@depth\char 1\relax\macc@set@skewchar\macc@nested@a 111{r}(\tau)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\alpha\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim\pi^{\operatorname{E}}}\left[\sum_{h=1}^{H}\log(\pi^{\operatorname{E}}(a_{h}|s_{h}))-\log(\widehat{\pi}(a_{h}|s_{h}))\right]+\alpha\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim\pi^{\operatorname{RL}}}\left[\sum_{h=1}^{H}\log(\pi^{\operatorname{E}}(a_{h}|s_{h}))-\log(\widehat{\pi}(a_{h}|s_{h}))\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>RL</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\alpha\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim\pi^{\operatorname{E}}}\left[\sum_{h=1}^{H}\log(\pi^{\operatorname{E}}(a_{h}|s_{h}))-\log(\widehat{\pi}(a_{h}|s_{h}))\right]+\alpha\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim\pi^{\operatorname{RL}}}\left[\sum_{h=1}^{H}\log(\pi^{\operatorname{E}}(a_{h}|s_{h}))-\log(\widehat{\pi}(a_{h}|s_{h}))\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\alpha\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim\pi^{\operatorname{E}}}\left[\sum_{h=1}^{H}\left|\log(\pi^{\operatorname{E}}(a_{h}|s_{h}))-\log(\widehat{\pi}(a_{h}|s_{h}))\right|\right]+\alpha\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim\pi^{\operatorname{RL}}}\left[\sum_{h=1}^{H}\left|\log(\pi^{\operatorname{E}}(a_{h}|s_{h}))-\log(\widehat{\pi}(a_{h}|s_{h}))\right|\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>RL</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\alpha\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim\pi^{\operatorname{E}}}\left[\sum_{h=1}^{H}\left|\log(\pi^{\operatorname{E}}(a_{h}|s_{h}))-\log(\widehat{\pi}(a_{h}|s_{h}))\right|\right]+\alpha\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim\pi^{\operatorname{RL}}}\left[\sum_{h=1}^{H}\left|\log(\pi^{\operatorname{E}}(a_{h}|s_{h}))-\log(\widehat{\pi}(a_{h}|s_{h}))\right|\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\alpha H\varepsilon_{\pi}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>π</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\alpha H\varepsilon_{\pi}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">We finish the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Outcome Reward Calculation</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a complete response <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, the outcome reward can be calculated as</p>
<table id="A3.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{r}(\tau)=\sum_{h=1}^{H}\widehat{r}(s_{h},a_{h})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{r}(\tau)=\sum_{h=1}^{H}\widehat{r}(s_{h},a_{h}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{r}(s_{h},a_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{r}(s_{h},a_{h})</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as in <a href="#S3.E10" title="In 3.3 The Endogenous Reward ‣ 3 Finding the Endogenous Reward Within the Language Model ‣ Generalist Reward Models: Found Inside Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>. We recognize that since language models generate text autoregressively, earlier tokens influence subsequent outputs. Thus, in our implementation, we compute the reward for a response as follows:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{r}(\tau)=\sum_{h=1}^{H}max\left(\gamma^{h-1},\beta\right)\widehat{r}(s_{h},a_{h})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{r}(\tau)=\sum_{h=1}^{H}max\left(\gamma^{h-1},\beta\right)\widehat{r}(s_{h},a_{h}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in(0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in(0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> is a discount factor and <math id="A3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. We use <math id="A3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=0.95,\beta=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.95</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=0.95,\beta=0</annotation></semantics></math> for experiments on Multifacted-Bench and for RL on the MATH-lighteval dataset, and <math id="A3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=0.93,\beta=0.03" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.93</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.03</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=0.93,\beta=0.03</annotation></semantics></math> for experiments on RM-bench. All sampling temperatures are set to <math id="A3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Prompt Templates</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The prompt templates of all methods used for benchmarking reward models on Multifacted-Bench <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lee et al., 2024b</a>]</cite> are shown below. As RM-Bench does not provide specific instructions for each sample, all methods use the default system prompt and the instructions in the <span id="A4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">User</span> part of the prompt templates will also be removed.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.F2" class="ltx_figure">
<p id="A4.F2.2" class="ltx_p">
<span id="A4.F2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" style="width:338.1pt;">
<span id="A4.F2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.F2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">System:</span></span>
<span id="A4.F2.2.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.F2.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">{instruction}</span></span>
<span id="A4.F2.2.1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.F2.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">User:</span></span>
<span id="A4.F2.2.1.4" class="ltx_p">### Query</span>
<span id="A4.F2.2.1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.F2.2.1.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">{query}
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span>
<span id="A4.F2.2.1.6" class="ltx_p">### Response</span>
<span id="A4.F2.2.1.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.F2.2.1.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">{response}</span></span>
</span></p>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 2: </span>Prompt template of our Endogenous Reward Model.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A4.F3" class="ltx_figure">
<p id="A4.F3.2" class="ltx_p">
<span id="A4.F3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" style="width:338.1pt;">
<span id="A4.F3.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.F3.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">System:</span></span>
<span id="A4.F3.2.1.2" class="ltx_p">You are an AI evaluator. Your role is to assess AI-generated text for its quality and adherence to instructions.</span>
<span id="A4.F3.2.1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.F3.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">User:</span></span>
<span id="A4.F3.2.1.4" class="ltx_p">You need to determine if the ‘Response’ is a good response to the ‘Query’, based on the standards set by the ‘Instruction’. A ‘good’ response MUST satisfy the following conditions:</span>
<span id="A4.F3.2.1.5" class="ltx_p">1. **Adherence to Instruction:** The answer’s tone, style, and content must perfectly match the provided instruction.</span>
<span id="A4.F3.2.1.6" class="ltx_p">2. **Relevance to Query:** The answer must directly and comprehensively address the user’s query without any irrelevant information.</span>
<span id="A4.F3.2.1.7" class="ltx_p">3. **Factuality and Helpfulness:** The information in the answer should be accurate and useful.</span>
<span id="A4.F3.2.1.8" class="ltx_p">Please carefully review the following materials.</span>
<span id="A4.F3.2.1.9" class="ltx_p">### Instruction</span>
<span id="A4.F3.2.1.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.F3.2.1.10.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">{instruction}
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span>
<span id="A4.F3.2.1.11" class="ltx_p">### Query</span>
<span id="A4.F3.2.1.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.F3.2.1.12.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">{query}
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span>
<span id="A4.F3.2.1.13" class="ltx_p">### Response</span>
<span id="A4.F3.2.1.14" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.F3.2.1.14.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">{response}
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span>
<span id="A4.F3.2.1.15" class="ltx_p">Based on your evaluation, is the answer a good response? Answer with only “YES” or “NO”.</span>
</span></p>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3: </span>Prompt template of Generative Verifier.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A4.F4" class="ltx_figure">
<p id="A4.F4.2" class="ltx_p">
<span id="A4.F4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" style="width:338.1pt;">
<span id="A4.F4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.F4.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">System:</span></span>
<span id="A4.F4.2.1.2" class="ltx_p">You are an AI evaluator. Your role is to assess AI-generated text for its quality and adherence to instructions.</span>
<span id="A4.F4.2.1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.F4.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">User:</span></span>
<span id="A4.F4.2.1.4" class="ltx_p">You are asked to evaluate two answers, ‘Response 1’ and ‘Response 2’, in relation to a ‘Query’ and a ‘Instruction’.</span>
<span id="A4.F4.2.1.5" class="ltx_p">**Evaluation Criteria:**</span>
<span id="A4.F4.2.1.6" class="ltx_p">1. **Adherence to Instruction:** Does the answer’s tone, style, and content align with the specified instruction?</span>
<span id="A4.F4.2.1.7" class="ltx_p">2. **Relevance to Query:** Does the answer directly and comprehensively address the user’s query?</span>
<span id="A4.F4.2.1.8" class="ltx_p">3. **Factuality and Helpfulness:** Is the information accurate and useful?</span>
<span id="A4.F4.2.1.9" class="ltx_p">Based on these criteria, please review the following:</span>
<span id="A4.F4.2.1.10" class="ltx_p">### Instruction</span>
<span id="A4.F4.2.1.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.F4.2.1.11.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">{instruction}
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span>
<span id="A4.F4.2.1.12" class="ltx_p">### Query</span>
<span id="A4.F4.2.1.13" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.F4.2.1.13.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">{query}
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span>
<span id="A4.F4.2.1.14" class="ltx_p">### Response 1</span>
<span id="A4.F4.2.1.15" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.F4.2.1.15.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">{response1}
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span>
<span id="A4.F4.2.1.16" class="ltx_p">### Response 2</span>
<span id="A4.F4.2.1.17" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.F4.2.1.17.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">{response2}
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span>
<span id="A4.F4.2.1.18" class="ltx_p">**Your Task:**</span>
<span id="A4.F4.2.1.19" class="ltx_p">Is ‘Response 2’ better than ‘Response 1’?</span>
<span id="A4.F4.2.1.20" class="ltx_p">**Rules for Your Response:**</span>
<span id="A4.F4.2.1.21" class="ltx_p">1. Respond with only “YES” or “NO”. Do not include explanations or any other text.</span>
<span id="A4.F4.2.1.22" class="ltx_p">2. “YES” means ‘Response 2’ is clearly better than ‘Response 1’.</span>
<span id="A4.F4.2.1.23" class="ltx_p">3. “NO” means ‘Response 2’ is not better (it is either worse or of equal quality) than ‘Response 1’.</span>
</span></p>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 4: </span>Prompt template of GenRM-Pairwise.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A4.F5" class="ltx_figure">
<p id="A4.F5.2" class="ltx_p">
<span id="A4.F5.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" style="width:338.1pt;">
<span id="A4.F5.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.F5.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">System:</span></span>
<span id="A4.F5.2.1.2" class="ltx_p">You are an AI evaluator. Your role is to assess AI-generated text for its quality and adherence to instructions.</span>
<span id="A4.F5.2.1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.F5.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">User:</span></span>
<span id="A4.F5.2.1.4" class="ltx_p">You need to evaluate the ‘Response’ in response to the ‘Query’, based on the ‘Instruction’. Your evaluation should be a score from 1 to 10.</span>
<span id="A4.F5.2.1.5" class="ltx_p">**Evaluation Criteria:**</span>
<span id="A4.F5.2.1.6" class="ltx_p">1. **Adherence to Instruction:** Does the answer’s tone, style, and content match the instruction?</span>
<span id="A4.F5.2.1.7" class="ltx_p">2. **Relevance to Query:** Does the answer directly and comprehensively address the user’s query?</span>
<span id="A4.F5.2.1.8" class="ltx_p">3. **Factuality and Helpfulness:** Is the information accurate and useful?</span>
<span id="A4.F5.2.1.9" class="ltx_p">Please review the following:</span>
<span id="A4.F5.2.1.10" class="ltx_p">### Instruction</span>
<span id="A4.F5.2.1.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.F5.2.1.11.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">{instruction}
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span>
<span id="A4.F5.2.1.12" class="ltx_p">### Query</span>
<span id="A4.F5.2.1.13" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.F5.2.1.13.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">{query}
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span>
<span id="A4.F5.2.1.14" class="ltx_p">### Response</span>
<span id="A4.F5.2.1.15" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.F5.2.1.15.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">{response}
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span>
<span id="A4.F5.2.1.16" class="ltx_p">Based on your assessment, provide a single integer score from 1 to 10.</span>
<span id="A4.F5.2.1.17" class="ltx_p">**Scoring Guide:**</span>
<span id="A4.F5.2.1.18" class="ltx_p">- **1-2:** Very Poor. Fails on most criteria.</span>
<span id="A4.F5.2.1.19" class="ltx_p">- **3-4:** Poor. Significant issues in multiple areas.</span>
<span id="A4.F5.2.1.20" class="ltx_p">- **5-6:** Average. Meets basic requirements but has clear flaws.</span>
<span id="A4.F5.2.1.21" class="ltx_p">- **7-8:** Good. Solid response with minor issues.</span>
<span id="A4.F5.2.1.22" class="ltx_p">- **9-10:** Excellent. A nearly perfect response that excels in all criteria.</span>
<span id="A4.F5.2.1.23" class="ltx_p">Provide only the numeric score.</span>
</span></p>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span>Prompt template of GenRM-Pointwise.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Samples of Generated Responses</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="A5.p1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Question:</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A5.p1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> be a positive real number such that all the roots of</span>
<span id="A5.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{3}+ax^{2}+ax+1=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{3}+ax^{2}+ax+1=0</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">are real. Find the smallest possible value of <math id="A5.p1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
</span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:100%;height:1px;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>
<span id="A5.p1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Qwen2.5-Math-7B:</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">To find the smallest possible value of <math id="A5.p1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> such that all the roots of the polynomial <math id="A5.p1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{3}+ax^{2}+ax+1=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{3}+ax^{2}+ax+1=0</annotation></semantics></math> are real, we will use the following steps:</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">1. First, let’s denote the roots of the polynomial by <math id="A5.p1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{1},r_{2},r_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1},r_{2},r_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>. By Vieta’s formulas, we know:</span>
<span id="A5.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{1}+r_{2}+r_{3}=-a," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1}+r_{2}+r_{3}=-a,</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{1}r_{2}+r_{2}r_{3}+r_{3}r_{1}=a," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1}r_{2}+r_{2}r_{3}+r_{3}r_{1}=a,</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{1}r_{2}r_{3}=-1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1}r_{2}r_{3}=-1.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">2. To ensure that all roots are real, we need to analyze the polynomial and its discriminant. For a cubic polynomial <math id="A5.p1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{3}+px^{2}+qx+r=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{3}+px^{2}+qx+r=0</annotation></semantics></math>, the discriminant <math id="A5.p1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> is given by:</span>
<span id="A5.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=18abcd-4b^{3}d+b^{2}c^{2}-4ac^{3}-27a^{2}d^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>18</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>27</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=18abcd-4b^{3}d+b^{2}c^{2}-4ac^{3}-27a^{2}d^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p6.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A5.p1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.p1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=a</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.p1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=a</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A5.p1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Substituting these values in, we get:</span>
<span id="A5.Ex50" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<span id="A5.Ex50X"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex50X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex50X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=18(1)(a)(a)(1)-4(a)^{3}(1)+(a)^{2}(a)^{2}-4(1)(a)^{3}-27(1)^{2}(1)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>18</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>27</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=18(1)(a)(a)(1)-4(a)^{3}(1)+(a)^{2}(a)^{2}-4(1)(a)^{3}-27(1)^{2}(1)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
<span id="A5.Ex50Xa"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex50Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=18a^{2}-4a^{3}+a^{4}-4a^{3}-27=a^{4}-8a^{3}+18a^{2}-27." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>18</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>27</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>18</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>27</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=18a^{2}-4a^{3}+a^{4}-4a^{3}-27=a^{4}-8a^{3}+18a^{2}-27.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">3. The discriminant <math id="A5.p1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> must be non-negative for the polynomial to have three real roots. So, we need to solve the inequality:</span>
<span id="A5.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{4}-8a^{3}+18a^{2}-27\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>18</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>27</mn></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{4}-8a^{3}+18a^{2}-27\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">4. To find the smallest possible value of <math id="A5.p1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>, we will solve the equation <math id="A5.p1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{4}-8a^{3}+18a^{2}-27=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>18</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>27</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{4}-8a^{3}+18a^{2}-27=0</annotation></semantics></math>. We can use numerical methods to find the roots of this polynomial. Let’s use Python to find the roots and determine the smallest positive real root.</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">“‘python</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">import numpy as np</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"># Define the polynomial coefficients</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p12.1" class="ltx_p">coefficients = <math id="A5.p1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[1,-8,18,0,-27]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>27</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[1,-8,18,0,-27]</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p13.1" class="ltx_p"># Find the roots of the polynomial</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p14.1" class="ltx_p">roots = np.roots(coefficients)</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p15" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p15.1" class="ltx_p">real_roots = [root.real for root in roots if np.isreal(root)]</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p16" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p16.1" class="ltx_p"># Filter out the positive real roots</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p17" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p17.1" class="ltx_p">positive_real_roots = [root for root in real_roots if root <math id="A5.p1.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>]</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p18" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p18.1" class="ltx_p"># Find the smallest positive real root</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p19" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p19.1" class="ltx_p">smallest_a = min(positive_real_roots)</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p20" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p20.1" class="ltx_p">print(smallest_a)</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p21" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p21.1" class="ltx_p">“‘</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p22" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p22.1" class="ltx_p">“‘output</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p23" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p23.1" class="ltx_p">0.0</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p24" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p24.1" class="ltx_p">“‘</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p25" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p25.1" class="ltx_p">It seems that the smallest positive real root found is <math id="A5.p1.p25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>, but we need to ensure that this value makes sense in the context of the problem. Let’s verify the polynomial and its discriminant again.</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p26" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p26.1" class="ltx_p">The polynomial <math id="A5.p1.p26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{3}+ax^{2}+ax+1=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{3}+ax^{2}+ax+1=0</annotation></semantics></math> must have all real roots, and the discriminant must be non-negative. For <math id="A5.p1.p26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=0</annotation></semantics></math>, the polynomial becomes <math id="A5.p1.p26.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{3}+1=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{3}+1=0</annotation></semantics></math>, which has roots <math id="A5.p1.p26.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=-1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.p1.p26.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=\frac{1+\sqrt{3}i}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=\frac{1+\sqrt{3}i}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A5.p1.p26.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=\frac{1-\sqrt{3}i}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=\frac{1-\sqrt{3}i}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. This means that <math id="A5.p1.p26.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=0</annotation></semantics></math> does not yield all real roots.</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p27" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p27.1" class="ltx_p">Let’s re-evaluate the polynomial and its discriminant more carefully. We need to find the smallest <math id="A5.p1.p27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> such that the discriminant is non-negative and all roots are real. We can use a different approach to find the smallest <math id="A5.p1.p27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p28" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p28.1" class="ltx_p">We can use a numerical method to find the smallest <math id="A5.p1.p28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> such that the discriminant is non-negative and all roots are real. Let’s use a bisection method to find the smallest <math id="A5.p1.p28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p29" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p29.1" class="ltx_p">“‘python</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p30" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p30.1" class="ltx_p">import numpy as np</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p31" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p31.1" class="ltx_p">from scipy.optimize import bisect</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p32" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p32.1" class="ltx_p"># Define the discriminant function</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p33" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p33.1" class="ltx_p">def discriminant(a):</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p34" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p34.1" class="ltx_p">return a⁢⁢4 - 8⁢a⁢⁢3 + 18⁢a⁢⁢2 - 27</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p35" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p35.1" class="ltx_p"># Use the bisection method to find the smallest positive root of the discriminant function</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p36" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p36.1" class="ltx_p">a_min = bisect(discriminant, 0, 10)</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p37" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p37.1" class="ltx_p"># Check the discriminant at the found value of a
discriminant_at_a_min = discriminant(a_min)</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p38" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p38.1" class="ltx_p">print((a_min, discriminant_at_a_min))</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p39" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p39.1" class="ltx_p">“‘</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p40" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p40.1" class="ltx_p">“‘output</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p41" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p41.1" class="ltx_p">(0.0, -27.0)</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p42" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p42.1" class="ltx_p">“‘</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p43" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p43.1" class="ltx_p">The output indicates that the smallest value of <math id="A5.p1.p43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> for which the discriminant is non-negative is approximately <math id="A5.p1.p43.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.0</annotation></semantics></math>, but the discriminant at this value is <math id="A5.p1.p43.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-27.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>27.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-27.0</annotation></semantics></math>, which means that <math id="A5.p1.p43.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=0</annotation></semantics></math> does not yield a valid solution for the polynomial to have all real roots.</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p44" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p44.1" class="ltx_p">Let’s refine our approach. We need to find the smallest positive value of <math id="A5.p1.p44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> such that the discriminant is non-negative and all roots are real. We can use a numerical method to find the smallest <math id="A5.p1.p44.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> such that the discriminant is non-negative and all roots are real.</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p45" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p45.1" class="ltx_p">We will use a bisection method to find the smallest <math id="A5.p1.p45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> such that the discriminant is non-negative and all roots are real. Let’s use a different range and a more precise method.</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p46" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p46.1" class="ltx_p">“‘python</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p47" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p47.1" class="ltx_p">import numpy as np</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p48" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p48.1" class="ltx_p">from scipy.optimize import bisect</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p49" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p49.1" class="ltx_p"># Define the discriminant function
def discriminant(a):
 return a**4 - 8*a**3 + 18*a**2 - 27</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p50" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p50.1" class="ltx_p"># Use the bisection method to find the smallest positive root of the discriminant function</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p51" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p51.1" class="ltx_p">a_min = bisect(discriminant, 1, 10)</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p52" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p52.1" class="ltx_p"># Check the discriminant at the found value of a
discriminant_at_a_min = discriminant(a_min)</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p53" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p53.1" class="ltx_p">print((a_min, discriminant_at_a_min))</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p54" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p54.1" class="ltx_p">“‘</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p55" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p55.1" class="ltx_p">“‘output</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p56" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p56.1" class="ltx_p">(1.0, -16.0)</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p57" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p57.1" class="ltx_p">“‘</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p58" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p58.1" class="ltx_p">Reach max function call limit.</span>
</span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:100%;height:1px;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>
<span id="A5.p1.p59" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p59.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p1.p59.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Qwen2.5-Math-7B (after RL with our EndoRM):</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p60" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p60.1" class="ltx_p">To find the smallest possible value of <math id="A5.p1.p60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> such that all the roots of the polynomial <math id="A5.p1.p60.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{3}+ax^{2}+ax+1=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{3}+ax^{2}+ax+1=0</annotation></semantics></math> are real, we can use the fact that the polynomial can be factored in a specific way.</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p61" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p61.1" class="ltx_p">First, we note that the polynomial <math id="A5.p1.p61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{3}+ax^{2}+ax+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{3}+ax^{2}+ax+1</annotation></semantics></math> can be written as <math id="A5.p1.p61.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{3}+ax^{2}+ax+1=(x+1)(x^{2}+(a-1)x+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{3}+ax^{2}+ax+1=(x+1)(x^{2}+(a-1)x+1)</annotation></semantics></math>. This factorization is valid because the roots of the polynomial must include -1 (since substituting <math id="A5.p1.p61.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=-1</annotation></semantics></math> into the polynomial gives <math id="A5.p1.p61.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-1)^{3}+a(-1)^{2}+a(-1)+1=-1+a-a+1=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-1)^{3}+a(-1)^{2}+a(-1)+1=-1+a-a+1=0</annotation></semantics></math>).</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p62" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p62.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we need to ensure that the quadratic polynomial <math id="A5.p1.p62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{2}+(a-1)x+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{2}+(a-1)x+1</annotation></semantics></math> has real roots. The discriminant of this quadratic polynomial must be non-negative. The discriminant <math id="A5.p1.p62.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A5.p1.p62.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{2}+(a-1)x+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{2}+(a-1)x+1</annotation></semantics></math> is given by <math id="A5.p1.p62.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a-1)^{2}-4\cdot 1\cdot 1=(a-1)^{2}-4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a-1)^{2}-4\cdot 1\cdot 1=(a-1)^{2}-4</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p63" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p63.1" class="ltx_p">For the quadratic to have real roots, we need <math id="A5.p1.p63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a-1)^{2}-4\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a-1)^{2}-4\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. This inequality can be solved as follows:</span>
<span id="A5.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a-1)^{2}\geq 4." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≥</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a-1)^{2}\geq 4.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p63.2" class="ltx_p">Taking the square root of both sides, we get:</span>
<span id="A5.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|a-1|\geq 2." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|a-1|\geq 2.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p63.3" class="ltx_p">This gives us two cases:</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p64" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p64.1" class="ltx_p">1. <math id="A5.p1.p64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a-1\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a-1\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, which simplifies to <math id="A5.p1.p64.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>.
2. <math id="A5.p1.p64.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a-1\leq-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a-1\leq-2</annotation></semantics></math>, which simplifies to <math id="A5.p1.p64.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\leq-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\leq-1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p65" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p65.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A5.p1.p65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> is a positive real number, we discard the second case and keep the first case. Therefore, the smallest possible value of <math id="A5.p1.p65.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> is 3.</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p66" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p66.1" class="ltx_p">Let’s verify this by checking if the polynomial <math id="A5.p1.p66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{3}+3x^{2}+3x+1=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{3}+3x^{2}+3x+1=0</annotation></semantics></math> has all real roots. The polynomial factors as <math id="A5.p1.p66.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x+1)(x^{2}+2x+1)=(x+1)(x+1)^{2}=(x+1)^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x+1)(x^{2}+2x+1)=(x+1)(x+1)^{2}=(x+1)^{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, which clearly has a triple root at <math id="A5.p1.p66.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=-1</annotation></semantics></math>, confirming that all roots are real.</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.p1.p67" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.p1.p67.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, the smallest possible value of <math id="A5.p1.p67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A5.p1.p67.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mn>3</mn></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{3}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
</span></span>
</div>
</section>
</article>
